era:Certificate
	a owl:Class ;
	rdfs:subClassOf vpa:Permission ;
	rdfs:label "Certificate"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Base class for those Certificates in the ERADIS register, which allow a IOD/SD described process."@en ;
	dcterms:created "2022-06-15"^^xsd:date ;
	dcterms:modified
		"2022-06-15"^^xsd:date ,
		"2024-10-24"^^xsd:date ,
		"2025-04-04"^^xsd:date
		;
	dcterms:source
		<http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2016/797/2020-05-28> ,
		<http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2016/798/2020-10-23>
		;
	rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
	owl:deprecated "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
	vs:term_status "stable" ;
	skos:scopeNote """In the context of the ERA vocabulary, a Certificate (`vpa:Permission`) can be:
- Safety Certificate (`vpa:grantedBy` NSA, `vpa:requestedBy` RailwayUndertaking), permitting 'access to the railway infrastructure' (SD Art. 10).
- Safety Authorisation (`vpa:grantedBy` NSA, `vpa:requestedBy` InfrastructureManager), permitting 'to manage and operate a rail infrastructure' (SD Art.12)
- Licence for the performance of rail transport services within the Union and the European Economic Area
- ECM Certificates, permitting to act as an ECM
- ...

Note: The `Interoperability documents` in ERADIS must use other Classes:
- EC DoV, EC DoC, EC DoSoU are issued by Applicants (use `era:ECDeclaration`);
- CLD's are issued by NoBo's (use `era:CLD`)"""@en ;
	.

era:CertificationLevelDocument
	a owl:Class ;
	rdfs:subClassOf vpa:EvidenceDocument ;
	rdfs:label "Certification Level Document"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Certification Level Document, as issued by a NoBo in the process of its certification/verification activities [RFU-STR-001]. The class can be reused as well for DeBo and AsBo certificates."@en ;
	era:usedInEradis "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
	dcterms:created "2025-04-04"^^xsd:date ;
	dcterms:modified "2025-11-23"^^xsd:date ;
	rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
	rdfs:seeAlso "https://nb-rail.eu/official-documents"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	owl:disjointWith era:ECDeclaration ;
	vs:term_status "stable" ;
	skos:altLabel "CLD"@en ;
	skos:scopeNote """Every CLD is the result of a process by a recognised/accredited body (`vpa:AppropriateBody`) which is allowed to issue it to a `vpa:RequestingBody` needing it for a specific purpose,
as defined in the IOD or SD. Several CLDs can support EC Declarations."""@en ;
	.

