era:etcs
	a owl:ObjectProperty ;
	rdfs:label "TSI compliant train protection system (ETCS)"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "European Train Control System (ETCS) application level supported by the track side equipment."@en ;
	era:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/Etcs> ;
	dcterms:created "2021-08-07"^^xsd:date ;
	dcterms:modified
		"2021-09-12"^^xsd:date ,
		"2024-08-13"^^xsd:date ,
		"2024-09-19"^^xsd:date ,
		"2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ,
		"2026-07-10"^^xsd:date
		;
	rdfs:domain [
		a owl:Class ;
		owl:unionOf (
			era:CommonCharacteristicsSubset
			era:RunningTrack
		) ;
	] ;
	rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
	rdfs:range era:ETCS ;
	vs:term_status "stable" ;
	skos:scopeNote '''It can be repeated as many times as the number of different ETCS levels are present.

For RDF data provision:
The value of this property is an instance of the era:ETCS, which has as properties the parameters 1.1.1.3.2.1 and 1.1.1.3.2.2.

For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, this property is the equivalent of the "Set" attribute, grouping parameters 1.1.1.3.2.1 and 1.1.1.3.2.2.

If the track is only equipped with a Class B system (i.e. no ETCS on the trackside), this must be reflected on the relevant Class B parameter (Parameter 1.1.1.3.5.3, era:protectionLegacySystem) and the era:etcs property is not applicable. In that case no era:ETCS resource is created; instead, the non-applicability is declared explicitly on the infrastructure element (e.g. the running track) with era:notApplicable era:etcs.'''@en ;
	.

