era:railInclination
	a
		owl:ObjectProperty ,
		owl:FunctionalProperty
		;
	rdfs:subPropertyOf
		era:trackObjParameter ,
		era:vehicleTypeTechnicalObjectCharacteristic
		;
	rdfs:label "Rail inclination"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "An angle defining the inclination of the head of a rail relative to the running surface."@en ;
	era:XMLName "ITP_RailInclination" ;
	era:applicable "Y" ;
	era:eratvIndex "4.6.5" ;
	era:formatNote "In XML the accepted value is NN, where N is a digit from 0 to 9."@en ;
	era:inSkosConceptScheme <http://data.europa.eu/949/concepts/rail-inclinations/RailInclinations> ;
	era:legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
	era:rinfIndex "1.1.1.1.4.3" ;
	era:shaclShapeValidationRule
		<http://data.europa.eu/949/eratv/shapes/RailInclination> ,
		<http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/InSkosConceptScheme> ,
		<http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/RailInclination> ,
		<http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/RailInclinationSKOS>
		;
	era:usedInRCCCalculations "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
	dcterms:created "2020-08-24"^^xsd:date ;
	dcterms:isRequiredBy
		<http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2019-06-16> ,
		<http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2021-05-18> ,
		<http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2023-09-08>
		;
	dcterms:modified
		"2022-10-20"^^xsd:date ,
		"2024-09-19"^^xsd:date ,
		"2025-02-14"^^xsd:date ,
		"2025-02-28"^^xsd:date
		;
	dcterms:source <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2014/1299/2023-09-28> ;
	rdfs:domain [
		a owl:Class ;
		owl:unionOf (
			era:CommonCharacteristicsSubset
			era:RunningTrack
			era:VehicleType
			era:VehicleTypeConfigParameterSet
		) ;
	] ;
	rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
	rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
	rdfs:seeAlso "INF TSI:4.2.4.7" ;
	vs:term_status "stable" ;
	skos:scopeNote
		"""This inclination is in most cases expressed for MS globally, but anyway it requires presentation for the specific track, when in one SoL more values occur.
An angle defining the inclination of the head of a rail when installed in the track relative to the plane of the rails (running surface), equal to the angle between the axis of symmetry of the rail (or of an equivalent symmetrical rail having the same rail head profile) and the perpendicular to the plane of the rails. The typical values for the railway inclination are 1:20, 1:30, 1:40."""@en ,
		"""[ERATV] This inclination is in most cases expressed for MS RINF globally, but anyway it requires presentation for the specific track, when in one SoL more values occur.

An angle defining the inclination of the head of a rail when installed in the track relative to the plane of the rails (running surface), equal to the angle between the axis of symmetry of the rail
 (or of an equivalent symmetrical rail having the same rail head profile) and the perpendicular to the plane of the rails. [NN] represents the denominator of the rail inclination expressed as 1/NN.
 The typical values are 1:20, 1:30, 1:40.

For a VehicleType, the value should currently be considered independent of a Vehicle Configuration."""@en
		;
	.

