era:shortestDistanceBetweenPantographsInContactWithOCL
	a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
	rdfs:subPropertyOf era:vehicleTypeTechnicalDataCharacteristic ;
	rdfs:label "Shortest distance between pantographs in contact with OCL"@en ;
	rdfs:comment "Shortest distance between two pantographs in contact with the OCL (to be indicated for each energy supply system the vehicle is equipped for; to be indicated for single and, if applicable, multiple operation) (only if number of raised pantographs is more than 1)."@en ;
	era:eratvIndex "4.10.8" ;
	era:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ShortestDistanceBetweenPantographsInContactWithOCL> ;
	era:unitOfMeasure unit:M ;
	dcterms:created "2020-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
	dcterms:modified
		"2021-09-15"^^xsd:date ,
		"2025-02-24"^^xsd:date ,
		"2025-06-24"^^xsd:date
		;
	rdfs:domain era:VehicleTypeConfigParameterSet ;
	rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
	rdfs:range xsd:string ;
	vs:term_status "stable" ;
	skos:editorialNote
		"Present and unchanged since <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665>"@en ,
		"Strings have the format: `Single: ___(; Multiple: ___)` (values in meter) and no StubClass is foreseen"@en
		;
	skos:scopeNote """The parameter is not applicable if `era:numberOfPantographsInContactWithOCL` < 2.

The parameter must have as range a VehicleTypeConfigParameterSet, of which the VehicleTypeConfiguration
at least contains one EnergySystem, from the ones recorded under `era:energySupplySystem`. Further, all of the ENE supply systems mentioned under that parameter
must have a value for this parameter `era:shortestDistanceBetweenPantographsInContactWithOCL`.

Parameter must be given also for multiple operation, if `era:maximumLocomotivesCoupled` > 1."""@en ;
	.

